# Document Processing Patterns

## pymupdf4llm (PDF to LLM-Ready Format)

- Use `to_markdown()` for RAG pipelines and LLM ingestion
- Use `to_json()` for custom pipelines needing bounding boxes
- Use `to_text()` for search indexing
- Set `page_chunks=True` for per-page metadata
- Table extraction enabled by default (ruled and borderless)
- Use `force_ocr=True` only for corrupt text layers
- Use `use_ocr=False` for text-only documents
- Process only needed pages with `pages` parameter
- Cache extraction results to disk after first run

## paddleocr (OCR Engine)

- Enable high-performance inference: `enable_hpi=True`
- Use TensorRT acceleration: `use_tensorrt=True` with CUDA 11.8+
- Use FP16 precision: `precision="fp16"`
- Tune `batch_size` based on GPU memory (default 30)
- Use mobile models (`PP-OCRv5_mobile`) for resource-constrained devices

## camelot-py (Table Extraction from PDFs)

- `flavor="lattice"`: Ruled tables with visible lines
- `flavor="stream"`: Borderless tables with whitespace-separated columns
- `flavor="network"`: Borderless tables via text-edge alignment (faster)
- `flavor="auto"`: Detects flavor per page
- Use `table_areas` for exact table boundaries
- Check `Table.parsing_report` confidence field

## ReportLab (PDF Generation)

- Use Platypus framework for high-level document layout
- Use Canvas API for low-level drawing
- Use `LongTable` for large datasets (streams to disk)
- Use `ProcessPoolExecutor` (not threads) for high-volume generation
- Pre-load fonts once before spawning workers
- Reuse styles: create `getSampleStyleSheet()` once per worker

## Pillow (Image Processing)

- Never set `Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS = None` (decompression bomb protection)
- Treat `DecompressionBombWarning` as error
- Validate file size, dimensions, and format before decoding
- Decode untrusted images in sandboxed subprocess with memory limits
- Never pass untrusted data to `ImageMath.eval()`
- Strip metadata from user-uploaded images before re-encoding
- Call `Image.close()` to release memory when done
- Convert color modes explicitly: `img.convert("RGB")` before saving as JPEG
